{
  "name": "NTC Thermostat Alarm (Green/Red)",
  "description": "An over-temperature alarm: an NTC thermistor bridge (the temperature rise/fall is modeled as the bridge output ramping 1.5→3.5→1.5V — the standard way to simulate a sensor electrically) feeds a Schmitt comparator (op-amp + positive feedback, ~265mV hysteresis band). Below threshold the green \"OK\" LED is lit (7.6mA, via a PNP high-side switch); past the trip point they swap — red \"ALARM\" lights (9.45mA) and green goes dark, with trip (2.64V) and release (2.38V) at different sensor voltages exactly as a real thermostat needs. (ngspice-validated.)",
  "tags": [
    "sensor",
    "temperature",
    "ntc",
    "thermostat",
    "alarm",
    "led",
    "comparator",
    "hysteresis"
  ],
